```systemverilog
typedef enum logic [1:0] {RD, WR, RMW} op_e;

class bus_cov;
  covergroup cg with function sample(op_e op, int unsigned len, bit [31:0] addr);
    option.per_instance = 1;
    cp_op  : coverpoint op;                    // one automatic bin per enum value
    cp_len : coverpoint len {
      bins one   = {1};
      bins small = {[2:15]};
      bins large = {[16:255]};
      illegal_bins too_big = {[256:$]};
    }
    cp_align : coverpoint addr[1:0] {
      bins aligned   = {0};
      bins unaligned = {[1:3]};
    }
    x_op_len : cross cp_op, cp_len;
  endgroup

  function new();
    cg = new();                 // an embedded covergroup must be created here
  endfunction

  function void write(bus_txn t);   // called once per completed transaction
    cg.sample(t.op, t.len, t.addr);
  endfunction
endclass
```

Sampling. `with function sample(...)` gives the covergroup an explicit sample method with arguments (§19.8.1), so it samples exactly once per transaction, with the values the monitor reconstructed, when the monitor calls `write`. Sampling on a clock (`covergroup cg @(posedge clk)`) instead counts every cycle, including idle ones, and samples signals rather than completed transactions.

Embedded covergroups must be constructed in the class's `new()`; if that assignment is missing, the covergroup does not exist and nothing is sampled, and assigning it anywhere else is illegal (§19.4).

Bins. `cp_op` gets one automatic bin per enum value (3). `cp_len` has 3 bins; a value of 256 or more triggers a run-time error, and illegal values are excluded from coverage (§19.5.6). Use `ignore_bins` instead when values are merely uninteresting, not wrong (§19.5.5).

Cross bins. `x_op_len` crosses 3 opcode bins with 3 length bins: 9 cross bins. Illegal bins are not part of the cross.

Other details: automatic bins are created only for 2-state values, and an integral coverpoint without explicit bins gets at most `auto_bin_max` bins, 64 by default (§19.5, §19.7). A `default` bin catches values outside the named bins but never counts toward coverage (§19.5).

